From: Charles <charles@e5>
Subject: [PATCH] sprd_wlan_combo: send the SC2355 recovery uevent from the wiphy device

wiphy_dev() is the wiphy's parent, the sprd-marlin3:wlan platform device: the
KOBJ_CHANGE with SC2355_RECOVERY=1 came as SUBSYSTEM=platform and never reached
/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/90-sc2355-recovery, which waits for an ieee80211/phyN
DEVPATH.  After a WCN firmware assert the radio was then never reopened: the
driver stayed at hif->exit, the AP up but silent.  Send it from the wiphy
device itself (SUBSYSTEM=ieee80211, DEVPATH .../ieee80211/phyN).

---
--- a/drivers/unisoc_platform/sprd_wlan_combo/common/cfg80211.c
+++ b/drivers/unisoc_platform/sprd_wlan_combo/common/cfg80211.c
@@ -275,7 +275,7 @@
 		if (hif->report_try == 1) {
 			char *env[] = { "SC2355_RECOVERY=1", NULL };
 
-			kobject_uevent_env(&wiphy_dev(priv->wiphy)->kobj,
+			kobject_uevent_env(&priv->wiphy->dev.kobj,
 					   KOBJ_CHANGE, env);
 		}
 		wl_info("Try to report assert a %d time \n", hif->report_try);
